<title>USA: Lehman names former Ecuador cenbank head economist.</title>
<headline>Lehman names former Ecuador cenbank head economist.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. investment bank Lehman Brothers Holdings Inc said Thursday that it had named Augusto de la Torre, former central bank governer of Ecuador, to be its chief Latin American economist.</p>
<p>De la Torre served as Ecuador's main central banker from 1993 until March 1997.</p>
<p>His responsibilities at Lehman Brothers will involve developing views on Latin American macroeconomics, the bank said.</p>
<p>(( Emerging Markets Desk, 212-859-1671))</p>
</text>
